#### 6.6.1 Line Shapes

Inherent limitations in the detectors lead to modifications of the invariant-mass line shape. Furthermore, material between the interaction region and the TPC can lead the daughter electrons to bremsstrahlung, creating a tail in the mass distribution. To model these effects, we simulate \(\Upsilon\) decays, run the results through GEANT to simulate detector effects, and embed the results in real data (see Sec. 6.3). Using our standard analysis maker, we can extract the embedded \(\Upsilon\).

